From 33213963309a86ec342f8dfa9c1c1c7cc46f5c6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 19:22:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0151 -- wave-55 PERF_MODE cut B2 (drop
 decorative FG detail) + A2 revert

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/PHASE11-WAVE-55-CONTRACT.md. Wave-55 is
the Track A Performance Mode Tier 1 cut B2, built on the PERF_MODE
env-var infrastructure banked in wave-54 patch 0150. ONE active
mechanism toggled by PERF_MODE: cut B2. The wave-55 patch also reverts
the wave-54 cut A2 (gain-collapsed on real HW); the A2 revert is dead-
code cleanup, not a second lever, so it rides in this one patch.

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: Cave Story is authored at GAME_FPS=50 but the
faithful render is measured-closed at ~30 fps on g2k. The 50 Hz
program's Track A trades render fidelity for raw fps behind the opt-in
PERF_MODE toggle; the faithful path stays the untouched production
default (PERF_MODE=0 -> byte-identical to wave-53 production).

CUT B2 -- DROP THE PURELY-DECORATIVE FG-OVER-SPRITE TILES:
The foreground tile pass (map_draw(TA_FOREGROUND)) draws the ~5.2 ms/
flip detail layer that renders OVER sprites (overhanging foliage,
foreground rocks the player walks behind). Under PERF_MODE>=1, B2
filters out the purely-decorative FG tiles.

B2 IS THE NARROWED CUT (NX?-2 resolution -- contract sec.3, nx-engine
STOP-and-ack audit 2026-05-16). B2 is NOT a full skip of the FG pass.
The vanilla tile-attribute table (tilekey.dat) freely OR's
TA_FOREGROUND with TA_SLOPE_* on real tilecodes, and map_draw()
strictly partitions tiles -- a TA_FOREGROUND tile draws ONLY in the FG
pass. A full FG-pass skip would therefore make every slope-FG tile
invisible-but-still-solid: the player would collide with slope geometry
they cannot see -- a gameplay defect, not a fidelity reduction. The
prior consolidated-plan "B2 confirmed safe" memo was UNDER-STATED -- it
verified collision .pxa DATA is untouched (true) but missed that an
FG-pass tile can itself BE visible collision geometry.

So B2 is a per-tile filter: new file-static helper _perf_b2_skip_fg_tile
drops a FG tile iff PERF_MODE>=1 AND the tile's attribute word is
EXACTLY TA_FOREGROUND (foreground is its SOLE attribute -> purely
decorative). ANY other bit set -- slope, solid, spikes, hurts, water,
current, destroyable -> attr != TA_FOREGROUND -> the tile is still
drawn. Exact equality is maximally conservative AND bit-value-agnostic
(no need to enumerate the TA_SLOPE_* sub-bits); it cannot create
invisible collision/hazard geometry by construction. The filter is
added at all 3 FG render partition sites in map.cpp
(_tilemap_render_plain_tiles_into_cache, _tilemap_render_special_tiles_
to_window, the _tilemap_render_tile_loop_impl template), each already
gating on (tileattr[t] & TA_FOREGROUND) == foreground. map_draw_oob()
is NOT gated -- it is a separate structural OOB-border edge-fill, not
decorative detail. The game.cpp MdsTilemapFgTimer scope is untouched so
[mds-decomp-stat phase=mds_tilemap_fg] keeps sample parity; on a B2
frame the bucket drops PARTIALLY (decorative tiles no longer drawn),
not to ~0 -- the residual is the collision-FG tiles + map_draw_oob.
The FG tilemap cache stays coherent: PERF_MODE is boot-constant so the
filtered FG layer caches deterministically per map.

Authoring note: the contract sec.1.1 sketched perf_b2_drop_fg() + an
inline per-tile expression; this consolidates the PERF_MODE check, the
exact-equality predicate, and the first-fire banner into one file-
static _perf_b2_skip_fg_tile() -- functionally identical to the
contract expression, one named function instead of an inline term
repeated 3x.

A2 REVERT: wave-54 cut A2 (backdrop-pinning) gain-collapsed on real HW
(-0.34 fps clean; the scrolling backdrop cost is the cache->window
blit, not the parallax re-render) and carried a black-valley visual
defect. This patch reverts the A2 hunk patch 0150 added to
map_draw_backdrop() -- the eff_scrolltype -> BK_FIXED routing block and
the A2 first-fire banner are removed; map_draw_backdrop() is byte-back
to its wave-53 production form. The PERF_MODE env-var infra patch 0150
added (perf_mode_level(), the sentinel cache, the perf-mode: level=N
boot banner) is RETAINED -- it is correct, measured-clean in wave-54,
and B2 depends on it.

CORRECTNESS: at PERF_MODE=0, perf_mode_level() is 0, _perf_b2_skip_fg_
tile() returns false for every tile, and the A2 code is gone -> the FG
pass and map_draw_backdrop() are bit-identical to the wave-53 / wave-54-
PERF_MODE=0 production render. build-qa ImageMagick AE=0 vs the wave-54
PERF_MODE=0 reference frames is the gate. PERF_MODE=1's missing
decorative FG detail IS the feature.

BANNERS for tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh: SWAP -- remove the wave-54
"perf-mode A2: backdrop pinned" regex (banner deleted with the A2
revert), add the B2 first-fire regex:
"perf-mode B2: decorative FG detail dropped (collision tiles kept)"
KEEP "perf-mode: level=[0-2]" (the infra banner, unchanged).

Slot 0151, append-only: patch 0150 stays committed/historical (shipped
in the wave-54 iter); 0151 reverts the 0150 A2 hunk + adds B2 + retains
the 0150 perf_mode_level infra.

FILES: src/map.cpp (A2 hunk reverted in map_draw_backdrop;
_perf_b2_skip_fg_tile helper added; B2 filter at 3 FG render sites;
perf_mode_level comment updated for wave-55).
